  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Group of two persons can be selected in <math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> ways. Let <math><msub><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> are together and <math><msub><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></math> are together. Let <math><msub><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> be the number of seats vacant at the left end, <math><msub><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> seats are between two pairs and <math><msub><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math> seats are vacant at the right end.<br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/44efb343-b0b7-4629-9e0d-d73c1ee8b2f9.png\" style=\"width:3.16667in;height:0.22014in\" /><br />We have,&nbsp;<math><msub><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo></math> where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0&nbsp;</mn><mi>and</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">w</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math><br />Number of ways of selecting seats <math><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi></mrow><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math><br />Persons can interchange their seats in <math><mn>2</mn><mo>!</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mo>×</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>!</mo></math> ways<br /><math><mo>⇒</mo></math> Required ways <math><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>×</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi></mrow><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>×</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>!</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mo>×</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>!</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>×</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi></mrow><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math>",
